WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.995
Step six finds the
Microsoft traffic profile

2
00:00:02.995 --> 00:00:05.862
with Learn's filtered
request and enables it.

3
00:00:05.862 --> 00:00:09.724
This writes to the test tenant,
and Module 6 rolls it back.

4
00:00:09.724 --> 00:00:13.123
Step seven assigns the pilot
group in the admin center,

5
00:00:13.123 --> 00:00:15.238
as an Application Administrator.

6
00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:19.192
Step eight turns on signaling and
records the setting to a file;

7
00:00:19.192 --> 00:00:21.626
signaling status should read enabled.

8
00:00:21.626 --> 00:00:23.650
Step nine is the validation.

9
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.484
On the pilot device, sign in to
SharePoint with the client running,

10
00:00:27.484 --> 00:00:32.100
then disable the client from the tray and
sign in again in a new browser session.

11
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.113
With source I P restoration, the two
sign-ins show the same I P address.

12
00:00:37.113 --> 00:00:38.537
Re-enable the client.

13
00:00:38.537 --> 00:00:42.228
Then, in the workspace, run
the guide's sign-in query:

14
00:00:42.228 --> 00:00:46.638
P C T through G S A is the share
of sign-ins the service carried.

15
00:00:46.638 --> 00:00:49.413
Run Module 1's freshness query again too.

16
00:00:49.413 --> 00:00:53.450
Keep the profile and signaling
on; Module 3 needs them.
